  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Prepositioning of in-kind food rations in lead up to UNSCR for vulnerable at risk populations in NWS.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WFP provides food assistance to 1.35 million people in Northwest Syria (NWS) through cross-border deliveries from Turkey that are authorised by the United Nations Security Council (UNSC) and managed by WFPs field office in Gaziantep, Turkey. On 12th July 2022, the authorisation of cross-border deliveries of humanitarian aid to the Syrian Arab Republic was renewed until 10 January 2023 Given the level of uncertainty associated with the upcoming renewal of UNSCR, WFP will employ the prepositioning of food supplies inside NWS as previously undertaken. A 1&#x2013;2-month implementation timeline is envisioned for this exercise- starting from October- including completion of CP handover of commodities by mid-December. This places the activities well within the UNSCR January 10th, 2023, deadline. This exercise is expected to sustain 1.35 million people for up to three months - beyond a potential non-extension of the resolution and ensure short term continuity of assistance whilst alternative measures are explored.</narrative>
  </description>
